:name: Demo board
:description: Sample script exercising the highlighting rules.
:Description metadata continues on lines that start with a colon,
:for example usart2<->usart3 passthrough between two machines.

# Variables: ?= only assigns when unset, so callers can override.
$name?="demo"
$bin?=@firmware/app.elf
$repl?=@$ORIGIN/platform.repl

using sysbus

mach create $name
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl
machine LoadPlatformDescription "C:/work/target/board.repl"

# Platform fragments can be given inline, in either quoting style.
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "bg96: Network.Quectel_BG96 @ usart2"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString 'dma: CoSimulated.CoSimulatedPeripheral @ sysbus <0x43c20000, +0x100> { frequency: 100000; 0 -> gic@31 }'
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString """
extraGpio: GPIOPort.MappedGpio @ sysbus 0x50000000
    numberOfPins: 8
    -> nvic@42
"""

sysbus LoadELF $bin
sysbus LoadHEX @../lib/bootloader.hex
sysbus.cpu PC 0x08000000
sysbus.cpu SP 0x20020000

// Renode also accepts '//' comments in scripts.
sysbus Tag <0x40080000 0x400> "RADIO"
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x40002C0C 0x80

# Backticks evaluate a Monitor expression and substitute its result.
$id = `next_value 1`
cpu VectorTableOffset `sysbus GetSymbolAddress "vectors"`

# Custom peripherals and their methods highlight like built-in ones.
sysbus.chipEvents SetControllerPort 18000
sysbus.chipEvents ResolvePort "Spi"
twi0.lsm9ds1_imu FeedAccelerationSample $ORIGIN/../tests/circle_rotated.data

emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal 3456 "term" false
connector Connect sysbus.uart0 term
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2

logLevel -1 sysbus.spi
sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.spi
logFile @/tmp/renode.log

machine StartGdbServer 3333
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.000100"
emulation SetAdvanceImmediately true

macro reset
"""
    pause
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
    sysbus.cpu PC 0x08000000
"""

runMacro $reset
start
